  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, equation of circle is $x^{2}+y^{2}+4 x+6 y-12=0$\r\nCentre $C(-2,-3)$ and radius $=\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+12}=5$\r\n$$\r\nx^{2}+y^{2}+4 x+6 y-12=0\r\n$$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\nC_{1} C_{2} &=\\sqrt{\\left(2+{2})^{2}+(-3+3)^{2}\\right.} \\\\\r\n&=\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+(0)^{2}}=4\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$\r\n$\\therefore$ Radius of circle, $S$\r\n$$\r\n=\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+({5})^{2}}=\\sqrt{16+25}=\\sqrt{41} \\text { unit }\r\n$$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2018_mat_a43.png\">",
